# Keep essential files for pull & run workflow:
# - data/raw/ (raw training data)
# - features/validation_sets/ (validation data)
# - features/aid_map.json (AID mapping)
# - features/aid_to_parent_law.json (parent law mapping)

# ============================================================================
# PULL & RUN WORKFLOW OPTIMIZATION
# ============================================================================

# Essential files that MUST be committed for pull & run:
# ✅ Source code: core/, app/, training/, evaluation/, data_processing/
# ✅ Configuration: config/, requirements.txt
# ✅ Entry points: run_workflow.py, run_app.py, setup_project.py
# ✅ Raw data: data/raw/
# ✅ Validation data: features/validation_sets/
# ✅ Essential mappings: features/aid_map.json, features/aid_to_parent_law.json
# ✅ Documentation: README.md, QUICK_START.md, *.md

# Generated files that are IGNORED (created by workflow):
# ❌ Models: models/, checkpoints/
# ❌ Processed data: features/processed_data_*/
# ❌ Indexes: features/faiss_index.bin, features/faiss_metadata.json
# ❌ Reports: reports/, logs/
# ❌ Virtual env: venv/

# User workflow after git pull:
# 1. python setup_project.py (creates venv, installs deps)
# 2. python run_workflow.py (trains models, creates indexes)
# 3. python run_app.py (launches Streamlit app)

# ============================================================================
# GIT MAINTENANCE FILES
# ============================================================================

